00:25:57,700 --> 00:26:03,680
The verb he uses to partner with Pasha is makah.

370
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:04,840
Everybody say makah.

371
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:10,320
Blot out or erase from the record my willful rebellion.

372
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:13,080
He's saying, take it off the pages of history.

373
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:16,960
Erase the sin, the rebellion that I have.

374
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:21,120
Next is avon, avon, yeah?

375
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:22,360
Cool.

376
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:25,440
Somebody, if anybody in here knows Hebrew, I'm really sorry.

377
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:25,880
All right.

378
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:27,620
Iniquity.

379
00:26:27,620 --> 00:26:30,400
This is what's translated iniquity.

380
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,900
It means to go astray.

381
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:37,900
And what Temaki pointed out here is that avon is either done intentionally or unintentionally.

382
00:26:37,900 --> 00:26:40,740
We can go astray on purpose, right?

383
00:26:40,740 --> 00:26:42,040
We can turn our back against God.

384
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:45,300
We can choose to go down the wide road that leads to destruction.

385
00:26:45,300 --> 00:26:47,640
Or we can just find ourselves getting lost.

386
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:51,420
Because we're just broken, sinful people.

387
00:26:51,420 --> 00:26:55,160
And one of the primary images of this in the Old Testament.

388
00:26:55,160 --> 00:27:03,760
So the result of avon, of going astray, either intentionally or unintentionally, is suffering and pain.

389
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:08,440
We live in a world full of suffering and pain.

390
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:17,680
And what most of us know from living in this world long enough is sometimes we have suffering and pain because we've intentionally gone astray from God's commands.

391
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:23,440
Anybody testify that they've gone astray from God's commands and had suffering in their life because of that?

392
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:34,020
And there are others of us in the room who have suffered and are suffering not as a result of any of our sin, but just because the world is broken.

393
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:38,480
We get diagnosis from the doctors.

394
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:42,140
We get the negative pregnancy test again and again and again.

395
00:27:42,140 --> 00:27:44,400
I don't know what it is for you, but many of us suffer.

396
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:45,800
And it's not because of our sin.

397
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:50,640
It's just because we live in a world that is pervaded by avon, pervaded by iniquity.

398
00:27:51,420 --> 00:27:54,800
And there's a real clear image of this in the Old Testament.

399
00:27:54,800 --> 00:28:00,400
The Old Testament uses one of the primary images of the suffering is leprosy.

400
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:05,960
And leprosy, some people get struck with leprosy in the Old Testament because they've gone astray.

401
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:09,480
Like because they've sinned, the result is they are struck with leprosy.

402
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:19,180
And many people in the Old Testament are covered with leprosy, even though they haven't seemingly done anything wrong to deserve the suffering.

403
00:28:19,180 --> 00:28:21,780
It just happens because we live in a broken world.

404
00:28:21,780 --> 00:28:27,540
He partners that with kavath, which is translated wash or clean up.

405
00:28:27,540 --> 00:28:34,240
He's saying, clean up the suffering in my life, whether through my own doing or because I live in a world that has gone astray from its original intent.

406
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:39,560
Lastly, katah, sin, which is a general term for moral failure.

407
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:44,480
This is the one we hear in Sunday school defined as missing the mark, right?

408
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:46,920
It's just this perpetual missing the target.

409
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:50,080
We are born in katah into a world marred by katah.

410
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:52,660
The result of this is ultimately death.

411
00:28:52,660 --> 00:28:57,020
So we've got intentional rebellion that leads to God's judgment.

412
00:28:57,020 --> 00:29:01,700
We've got either intentional or unintentional going astray that leads to suffering.

413
00:29:02,860 --> 00:29:06,820
And we've got just the perpetual missing the mark that leads to death.

414
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:12,140
Death is ultimately the consequence of our sin before a holy God.

415
00:29:12,380 --> 00:29:14,980
And the Hebrew word he partners with there is taher.

416
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:19,880
It means to cleanse or to make me acceptable in your presence.

417
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:30,320
Now, all three of these words for our sin and God's making a way out of the consequences of our sin culminate in one final Hebrew word.

