00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:51,100
So, are you guys good with me so far?

423
00:29:51,100 --> 00:29:51,880
All right.

424
00:29:51,880 --> 00:29:55,060
De-sin my sin.

425
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:57,900
Take away all the consequences of my sin.

426
00:29:57,900 --> 00:30:00,100
The judgment of my willful rebellion.

427
00:30:00,100 --> 00:30:02,980
The suffering of a world gone astray.

428
00:30:02,980 --> 00:30:05,680
The death of a world in moral decay.

429
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:14,580
De-sin all of the consequences of the sin that pervades my life, whether through my own decision or just through the reality of living in a broken world.

430
00:30:14,580 --> 00:30:17,900
If you are a God who moves towards us, God, forgive us.

431
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:19,780
De-sin our sin.

432
00:30:19,780 --> 00:30:20,720
My rebellion.

433
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:21,840
Take away my judgment.

434
00:30:21,840 --> 00:30:25,900
For the suffering that I have brought about in the lives of others.

435
00:30:25,900 --> 00:30:27,700
Wash it away.

436
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:30,600
For the death of a world in moral decay.

437
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:31,700
Resurrect it.

438
00:30:32,580 --> 00:30:35,880
He says, de-sin my sin with hyssop.

439
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:42,560
This word is used in three main ways in the Old Testament, and it's used once in the New Testament.

440
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:46,600
The first way it's used in the Old Testament is the story of the Passover.

441
00:30:46,600 --> 00:30:47,680
Anybody remember that?

442
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:53,860
We spread the blood of an innocent lamb over the doorpost with hyssop.

443
00:30:53,860 --> 00:30:57,720
This is the substitutionary removal of God's judgment.

444
00:30:57,720 --> 00:31:05,320
God is passing over the judgment of his Hebrew people because of the blood of the innocent lamb.

445
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:06,900
He's taking away judgment.

446
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:13,800
The second, hyssop is used in a process in the tabernacle when washing those who have been cleansed with leprosy.

447
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:20,220
God is taking away the suffering of a world gone astray.

448
00:31:20,220 --> 00:31:30,360
Lastly, it's used in a process of cleansing those who have come in contact with a dead body so that they can come back into the presence of God in the tabernacle.

